  "chunks": [
    {
      "text": "Paper Water",
      "start": 0.0,
      "duration": 1.85
    },
    {
      "text": "An ink pond, alive to a small gesture.",
      "start": 2.03,
      "duration": 3.5
    },
    {
      "text": "Fish drift across a field of textured paper. Their bodies hold different amounts of ink: fine contours, soft grey washes, dark patches. Leaves float at the edges. Shapes below the surface fade into the page.",
      "start": 5.71,
      "duration": 14.475
    },
    {
      "text": "The fish move through their own rhythms of swimming, coasting, and small bursts of speed. They sometimes gather and sometimes wander apart. Click or tap to drop a few blots of food. Nearby fish approach, rise, and take small bites. A mouth opens, a ripple spreads, and the pond begins to settle again.",
      "start": 20.365,
      "duration": 20.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Paper Water holds a drawing in motion. Its depth comes through changes in definition, pigment, and the slight distortion of the water. The viewpoint stays still while the life within it continues.",
      "start": 40.545,
      "duration": 13.45
    },
    {
      "text": "By Brad Necyk, 2026. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
      "start": 54.175,
      "duration": 6.075
    }
  ],
